{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>As I have commanded you.</b> From here our Rabbis said in tractate Ḥullin: this teaches that Moses was commanded concerning the windpipe and the gullet, and concerning one majority in fowl and two majorities in animal. And Rabbi Ya'akov of Corbeil said: כאשר צויתיך — it comes to teach one majority in fowl and two majorities in animal. Examine it and you will find. Another explanation: אש\"ר — alef [is] one, shin [is] two, resh [is] rov ['majority']. And clarify the minority in that whose slaughter is minimal — that is, in fowl. Thus one in fowl and two in animal, and rov applies to both of them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "In the acronym אש\"ר, each Hebrew letter name is taken to encode a number and a concept: alef=1 (one majority, fowl), shin=2 (two majorities, animal), resh=rov (majority). 'ונוקי' read as 'and clarify' (from לנקוט), interpreting the mnemonic as: identify which slaughter requires the lesser requirement."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:55.051225431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}